{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536154-mimicking-simulating-other-splats-with-magic","id":1536154,"title":"Mimicking/simulating other splats with magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-23T07:07:27-07:00","id":1536154,"title":"Mimicking/simulating other splats with magic","content":"Is it possible to emulate other splats' powers with the right Arcana?<br /> <br /> As an example, to &quot;become&quot; a Werewolf using a mix of Life, Spirit, or something else? I know you would not become an Uratha per se, with all the cultural baggage, etc. But having access to the shapeshifting ability, fast healing, improved senses, etc.<br /> <br /> Could a mage become a half-spirit/half-flesh being?<br /> <br /> Has anyone tried that before? (And not only werewolves, but also vampires, changelings, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T08:07:47-07:00","id":1536155,"title":"","content":"You can find those answer in Contagion Chronicle player guide, also shouldn't this be in Mage the Awakening forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T10:56:04-07:00","id":1536158,"title":"","content":"Well, mages are really good at examining things. If we are discussing ways to achieve this, there is a rare Coil(from Vampire the Requiem) that has a ritual of grafting parts of other supernaturals and getting access to their powers.<br /> <br /> I'd say that a mage that somehow got access to this knowledge and got to study this mystery could probably develop something similar to steal other supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> But if we are trying to emulate things, Werewolf and Sin-Eater would probably be the easiest because the Spirt and Death arcanas already govern Spirits and Ghosts. The power of Kindred Disciplines could be a little tricky depending on the Discipline, but there are some that can be pretty easy recreated with Mind(Dominate, Obfuscate and Nightmare).<br /> <br /> Contracts from changeling could be a little tricky, but maybe using some sort of Fate spell to channel Glamour into your pattern(mages already can do that with essence) and them getting some way of translating your Gnosis into Wyrd, similar to how you can already do that for Supernal beings so changelings can make deal for Contracts with them.<br /> <br /> If we are just trying to pass as other supernatural being, I think Mind alone could do the trick, since it's about other peoples perception you can create an illusion of beign that Splat you are trying to emulate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T18:54:05-07:00","id":1536181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536154-mimicking-simulating-other-splats-with-magic#post1536154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But having access to the shapeshifting ability, fast healing, improved senses, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, each of those things is going to be the result of a spell. Well, improved healing (but nowhere near werewolf good) and senses might go together under Body Control, I'd have to check. But something like shapeshifting will be &quot;you cast the spell that modifies your shape one time&quot;, rather than casting a spell that lets you reflexively go back and forth between multiple shapes (or even just human and animal).<br /> <br /> That alone is going to be subject to limitations of spell control. Depending on how many spells it takes to emulate the thing you want, you may start wracking up Paradox fast.<br /> <br /> Awakened magic before archmastery is also not great at creating something like innately supernatural beings that aren't directly under the purview of an Arcanum, and even that might have some limits. The Spirit Arcanum might handily turn you into a regular spirit (although a lot of the stats might have limitations based on spell potency), but not the more wild permutations of that type, let alone something original.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone tried that before? (And not only werewolves, but also vampires, changelings, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>In character, yes mages do sometimes try to transform themselves into inhuman things, albeit in ways that go a bit beyond modification by spell casting (and that aren't quite well modelled under the rules).<br /> <br /> The result is almost invariably that they break their own souls in the process and become Enraptured.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T08:08:28-07:00","id":1536361,"title":"","content":"Or a Lich...<br /> <br /> Creating a legacy based around certain abilities (like shape-shifting, healing, etc) would he the easiest way to mechanically overcome some of the limits <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> points out.<br /> <br /> Automatic success on a shape-shifting power with it not being a spell would be fairly effective. No counter spell, but you also don't invoke Quiescense or whatever it is werewolves cause (Primal fear?) So it has social downsides...<br /> <br /> aA life/spirit legacy could do most of what a werewolf can.<br /> <br /> Mimicing a Sin-Eater would be possible, but getting an actual Geist and making a deal with them (not the bargain) could actually be more effective...<br /> <br /> Mimicing a Demon or Mummy might he difficult, depending on which features you wanted to copy.<br /> <br /> Not sure about a Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T11:55:57-07:00","id":1536374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536154-mimicking-simulating-other-splats-with-magic?p=1536361#post1536361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a Lich...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, some elaboration could be used with there.<br /> <br /> Archons (as DaveB has given the name for them elsewhere) might be regarded as a bit of a middle ground between &quot;you can use the Arcana to turn yourself into a normal example of ephemeral entities that fall directly under the Arcana&quot; and &quot;you can organically become a non-human entity entirely&quot;. While being a spirit, ghost, or goetia who still possesses full spellcasting capability does constitute something a bit more elaborate and invested than just using a simple Patterning spell on yourself, you might not quite get the full range of capabilities of those beings, and they're still somewhat simpler in form than many other kinds of supernatural being. The main benefit is the immortality.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose there might be implications that there are some more obscure paths to becoming a Lich that entail some loss of humanity (as part of the whole &quot;divesting yourself of an essential human trait essentially makes you less human). Still, those are probably not as direct as becoming more like an established type, and might carry more risk of just going Rapt along the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Automatic success on a shape-shifting power with it not being a spell would be fairly effective. No counter spell, but you also don't invoke Quiescense or whatever it is werewolves cause (Primal fear?) So it has social downsides...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not causing a breaking point is a downside?<br /> <br /> (Werewolves inflict Lunacy)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">aA life/spirit legacy could do most of what a werewolf can.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Most</i> of what a werewolf can?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that werewolves can do more than ten things.<br /> <br /> And can also do several things that don't really fall under either of those Arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mimicing a Sin-Eater would be possible, but getting an actual Geist and making a deal with them (not the bargain) could actually be more effective...</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: can Geists use the same powers as Sin-Eaters by themselves, or are they just stuck with Numina and Influences and need to substitute for a human soul to get all the cool stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T13:12:05-07:00","id":1536379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536154-mimicking-simulating-other-splats-with-magic?p=1536374#post1536374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: can Geists use the same powers as Sin-Eaters by themselves, or are they just stuck with Numina and Influences and need to substitute for a human soul to get all the cool stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Bound geist, when Unleashed, uses its Sin-Eater's Haunts with a dicepool of Power + Rank + Haunt and uses Influences of its innate Key(s) equal to its Rank. Unbound geists use Numina and Influence over their innate Key as normal and may presumably benefit from knowledge of Ceremonies like other ghosts can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Mixed up 1e and 2e power terms. 05-27-2024, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T14:26:29-07:00","id":1536384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536154-mimicking-simulating-other-splats-with-magic?p=1536379#post1536379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Bound geist, when Unleashed, uses its Sin-Eater's Haunts with a dicepool of Power + Rank + Haunt and uses Influences of its innate Key(s) equal to its Rank. Unbound geists use Numina and Influence over their innate Key as normal and may presumably benefit from knowledge of Ceremonies like other ghosts can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean that a mage who has made an association with one is getting a bit more out of it than they would a ghost*, but still a decent amount less than a proper Sin-Eater would?<br /> <br /> * Although it sounds like even regular ghosts run through the elaborations of that game end up with more than both blue book and core Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T16:10:25-07:00","id":1536390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536154-mimicking-simulating-other-splats-with-magic?p=1536384#post1536384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean that a mage who has made an association with one is getting a bit more out of it than they would a ghost*, but still a decent amount less than a proper Sin-Eater would?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd functionally be getting what you'd get out of granting a moderately powerful Goetia Manifestations through the Death Arcanum, plus theoretical access to Skills, Merits, and some amount of teachable magical ritual gated behind an overall inability to communicate in either direction save through the context of fear and intimidation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T01:17:41-07:00","id":1536556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536154-mimicking-simulating-other-splats-with-magic#post1536154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to emulate other splats' powers with the right Arcana?<br /> <br /> As an example, to &quot;become&quot; a Werewolf using a mix of Life, Spirit, or something else? I know you would not become an Uratha per se, with all the cultural baggage, etc. But having access to the shapeshifting ability, fast healing, improved senses, etc.<br /> <br /> Could a mage become a half-spirit/half-flesh being?<br /> <br /> Has anyone tried that before? (And not only werewolves, but also vampires, changelings, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can cast spells; those spells can have effects like fast healing, improved senses, change shape, etc. However, those do not <i>give powers. Y</i>ou cannot cast a spell which would allow you to turn into wolf and then back to human whenever you like it; you can cast a spell which turns you into a wolf, and then dismiss it and turn back into human. Arguably spells which turn you into ephemeral beings <i>can</i> give you Numina and Influences (I've written a Forge Numen spell, which does exactly that), but those are exceptions to the rule, because &quot;spirits&quot; and &quot;ghosts&quot; are parts of Spirit and Death Arcana, respectively; vampires and werewolves are <b>not</b> parts of them in the same way, because you cannot cast a spell &quot;Create Vampire&quot; like you can cast &quot;Create Ghost&quot;. So mages don't really <i>gain</i> their powers; they <i>imitate</i> them with spells. Not to say such imitations are always inferior (in many case they are evidently not), but they do not have the same essential and symbolic nature - which means a lot in Mage universe. Ultimately, shapeshifter mages are not the same type of shapeshifters as Uratha are, and so on. For that to happen, you need Entities Practice, at which point the distinction is meaningless anyway - archmages do as they will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}